The failure was the audit sandbox’s PID/procfs mismatch: Lean 4.22 asks for `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, while only `/proc/self` names the sandboxed process correctly. A minimal preload shim maps `getpid()` to the procfs-visible PID; the pinned Lean and Lake versions now start, and I’m rerunning the unchanged trusted `check_generation` call with that documented infrastructure workaround.
